 "rule": "Every key closes one row wire and one column wire. Three keys held in an L (two share a row, and one of those shares a column with the third) make the keyboard also see the fourth corner of that rectangle closed. If a key sits at the fourth corner, the keyboard cannot tell whether it is pressed, so it drops the combination. If the fourth corner is an empty spot, all three register. Up to 6 keys register together when no three of them are dropped; the keyboard never registers more than 6 keys at once (6-key rollover).",
 "rollover": 6,
